{"id": "unknown-2026-11-27-012", "date": "2026-11-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Japan’s 30th solar auction allocates 27.7 MW of PV capacity", "content": "<p>Japan has selected seven PV projects ranging in size from 500 kW to 20 MW in its latest procurement exercise. The lowest bid came in at JPY 5.00 ($0.031)/kWh, while the weighted average final price reached JPY 9.13/kWh.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/japans-30th-solar-auction-allocates-27-7-mw-of-pv-capacity/\">Japan’s 30th solar auction allocates 27.7 MW of PV capacity</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/japans-30th-solar-auction-allocates-27-7-mw-of-pv-capacity/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-27-013", "date": "2026-11-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Greenhushing, PV prices, battery prices and the shifting bottleneck", "content": "<p>Greenhushing reflects a shift towards prioritising environmental performance over public sustainability commitments, as declining solar PV and battery costs strengthen the economic case for corporate decarbonisation. The solar industry’s next phase of growth will depend less on equipment affordability and more on grid access, system flexibility, integration and long-term operational value.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/greenhushing-pv-prices-battery-prices-an", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/greenhushing-pv-prices-battery-prices-and-the-shifting-bottleneck/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-27-014", "date": "2026-11-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: BP, Iberdrola start operations at Spain’s largest green hydrogen plant", "content": "<p>In other news, Australia and Germany are exploring hydrogen-based aviation, while Envision Energy and Greensteel Australia are considering a 400 MW green hydrogen system for low-carbon steelmaking.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/the-hydrogen-stream-bp-iberdrola-start-operations-at-spains-largest-green-hydrogen-plant/\">The Hydrogen Stream: BP, Iberdrola start operations at Spain’s largest green hydrogen plant</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazi", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/the-hydrogen-stream-bp-iberdrola-start-operations-at-spains-largest-green-hydrogen-plant/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-27-015", "date": "2026-11-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh makes solar equipment recycling mandatory", "content": "<p>Bangladesh’s new Special Solar Power Installation Act requires manufacturers, suppliers and service providers to implement take-back schemes for end-of-life solar equipment, marking a step toward sustainable PV waste management.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/bangladesh-makes-solar-equipment-recycling-mandatory/\">Bangladesh makes solar equipment recycling mandatory</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/bangladesh-makes-solar-equipment-recycling-mandatory/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-27-016", "date": "2026-11-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Elco launches propane air-to-water heat pumps for commercial applications", "content": "<p>The new heat pump series is available in seven versions with heating capacities ranging from 40.1 kW to 84.4 kW and seasonal coefficients of performance of up to 4.70. The systems can deliver flow temperatures of up to 75 C and be cascaded to reach a combined capacity of 1.35 MW.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/elco-launches-propane-air-to-water-heat-pumps-for-commercial-applications/\">Elco launches propane air-to-water heat pumps for commercial applications</a", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/27/elco-launches-propane-air-to-water-heat-pumps-for-commercial-applications/", "type": "rss"}]}
